    "verdict": "WMI repository corruption. Many MECM client functions depend on a healthy WMI repository, so the failure surfaces across multiple components at once.",
    "evidence": [
        { "component": "ccmsetup", "match": "WMI" },
        { "component": "CcmExec", "match": "provider" }
    ],
    "fix": "Run `winmgmt /verifyrepository` on the client. If inconsistent, attempt `winmgmt /salvagerepository` first. Use `/resetrepository` only as a last resort: a reset destroys the CCM namespace and requires a full client reinstall via ccmsetup.",
    "references": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/troubleshoot/windows-server/system-management-components/rebuild-wmi-repository",
